      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "9:84",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلَىٰٓ أَحَدࣲ مِّنۡهُم مَّاتَ أَبَدࣰ ا وَلَا تَقُمۡ عَلَىٰ قَبۡرِهِۦٓۖ إِنَّهُمۡ كَفَرُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَمَاتُواْ وَهُمۡ فَٰسِقُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "At-Tawba",
      "literal_gloss": "his grave",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And do not pray [the funeral prayer, O Muhammad], over any of them who has died - ever - or stand at his grave. Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were defiantly disobedient.",
        "pickthall": "And never (O Muhammad) pray for one of them who dieth, nor stand by his grave. Lo! they disbelieved in Allah and His messenger, and they died while they were evil-doers.",
        "khattab": "And do not ever offer ˹funeral˺ prayers for any of their dead, nor stand by their grave ˹at burial˺, for they have lost faith in Allah and His Messenger and died rebellious",
        "arberry": "And pray thou never over any one of them when he is dead, nor stand over his grave; they disbelieved in God and His Messenger, and died while they were ungodly."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        22,
        7,
        12
      ],
      "form_arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورِ",
      "lemma": "qabor",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَبْر",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "22:7",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَأَنَّ ٱلسَّاعَةَ ءَاتِيَةࣱ لَّا رَيۡبَ فِيهَا وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَبۡعَثُ مَن فِي ٱلۡقُبُورِ",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Hajj",
      "literal_gloss": "the graves",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And [that they may know] that the Hour is coming - no doubt about it - and that Allah will resurrect those in the graves.",
        "pickthall": "And because the Hour will come, there is no doubt thereof; and because Allah will raise those who are in the graves.",
        "khattab": "And certainly the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it. And Allah will surely resurrect those in the graves",
        "arberry": "and because the Hour is coming, no doubt of it, and God shall raise up whosoever is within the tombs."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        35,
        22,
        16
      ],
      "form_arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورِ",
      "lemma": "qabor",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَبْر",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "35:22",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَمَا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡأَحۡيَآءُ وَلَا ٱلۡأَمۡوَٰتُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُسۡمِعُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ بِمُسۡمِعࣲ مَّن فِي ٱلۡقُبُورِ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Faatir",
      "literal_gloss": "the graves",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And not equal are the living and the dead. Indeed, Allah causes to hear whom He wills, but you cannot make hear those in the graves.",
        "pickthall": "Nor are the living equal with the dead. Lo! Allah maketh whom He will to hear. Thou canst not reach those who are in the graves.",
        "khattab": "Nor are the dead and the living equal. Indeed, Allah ˹alone˺ makes whoever He wills hear, but you ˹O Prophet˺ can never make those in the graves hear ˹your call˺",
        "arberry": "not equal are the living and the dead. God makes to hear whomsoever He will; thou canst not make those in their tombs to hear -"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        60,
        13,
